      "limitations": "The study formed 12 novel flocks of four adult males in two age classes. Individual contact calls were recorded in separate 55-minute sessions, with the focal bird in a sound-isolation chamber, visually but not acoustically connected to flockmates. Social behavior was captured in separate 80-minute video sessions of the newly formed experimental flocks; early-morning sessions were coded for interactions and both sessions for proximity. The deposit provides derived call features and social codes with overlapping flock/date/block metadata, but no source call audio or shared call/event timestamps. This cannot support event-level sound-to-behavior prediction. The 12-flock design and age treatment constrain generalization. The README documents an interobserver workbook with a subset recoded by a second observer, but that workbook has not been inspected and no agreement value is claimed.",
